# Component Development Standards

## Component Architecture
Follow the established component structure in the project:

```
src/components/
├── ui/ (shadcn/ui base components)
├── layout/ (Header, Footer, Sidebar, ResponsiveSidebar)
├── home/ (AboutPreview, CTASection, HeroSection, ProjectsPreview)
├── projects/ (ProjectCard, ProjectDetail, ProjectImage, ProjectVideo)
├── contact/ (ContactForm)
├── animations/ (PointSphere, RotatingText)
└── common/ (BackToTop, shared utilities)
```

## Component Guidelines
- Use functional components with TypeScript interfaces for all props
- Implement proper error boundaries and loading states
- Follow the existing naming conventions and file organization
- Use shadcn/ui components as base building blocks when possible
- Ensure all components are responsive and accessible

## Animation Components
- Three.js components should be wrapped in React.Suspense with fallbacks
- Use React.memo for performance optimization on animation-heavy components
- Implement cleanup functions in useEffect for Three.js scenes
- Make particle counts responsive based on device capabilities

## Form Components
- Use controlled components with proper validation
- Implement loading and error states for form submissions
- Ensure proper accessibility with labels, ARIA attributes, and keyboard navigation
- Follow the existing EmailJS integration pattern

## Styling Guidelines
- Use Tailwind CSS classes with the established design system
- Leverage CSS custom properties for theme consistency
- Implement responsive design with mobile-first approach
- Use Framer Motion for page transitions and micro-interactions

## Performance Requirements
- Lazy load non-critical components
- Optimize images with Next.js Image component
- Implement proper code splitting for heavy components
- Monitor bundle size and performance metrics# Component Development Standards

